  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two backends, not one thing",
      "items": [
        "Databricks-backed scopes are portable — recreate the scope, re-put the values",
        "Key Vault-backed scopes have no AWS or GCP equivalent as a Databricks backend",
        "Moving off Azure means every Key Vault-backed scope becomes Databricks-backed or reads the vault directly from application code"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What the decision step actually decides",
      "items": [
        "Re-issue from the system of record whenever one exists — the best case, not the exception",
        "A source-cloud credential does not migrate; that access becomes a storage credential instead",
        "An unrecognized secret is escalated now, because it is exactly what stops a cutover later"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The forgotten step fails at run time, not deploy time",
      "items": [
        "A scope is created with MANAGE for its creator and nothing else",
        "Without an explicit READ grant, dbutils.secrets.get fails inside the job, not at bundle deploy",
        "Grant to the job's run-as identity — often a service principal, not the person testing"
      ]
    }
  ]
}